---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const pageTitle = "Terms of Service — BriskRead";
const pageDescription = "Terms of Service and usage guidelines for BriskRead web speed reading tools and lifetime subscriptions.";
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <section class="terms-section mt-8">
    <div class="container max-w-xl">
      <div class="glass content-card">
        <h1>Terms of service</h1>
        <p class="muted">Last Updated: July 17, 2026</p>

        <div class="content mt-6">
          <p>
            Welcome to BriskRead! By accessing our website at briskread.com, you agree to comply with and be bound by the following terms and conditions of use.
          </p>

          <h2>1. Use License & Intellectual Property</h2>
          <p>
            BriskRead provides a web-based client-side reader tool. Permission is granted to temporarily load the web app for personal, non-commercial transitory reading.
          </p>
          <p>
            You may not:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Attempt to decompile, reverse-engineer, or maliciously extract code from the speed-reading engine.</li>
            <li>Use URL extraction or other capture tools to scrape copyrighted web assets in automated bulk.</li>
            <li>Resell or redistribute premium features under a different brand name.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>2. Disclaimer of Warranty</h2>
          <p>
            BriskRead is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. We make no warranties, expressed or implied, and hereby disclaim and negate all other warranties including, without limitation, implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement of intellectual property.
          </p>
          <p>
            Because all document parsing, image OCR, and speech narration occur client-side, BriskRead does not guarantee that file parsing will be error-free or compatible with every corrupt EPUB or scanned PDF structure.
          </p>

          <h2>3. Lifetime Premium Membership</h2>
          <p>
            If you upgrade to the Pro lifetime membership:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Lifetime Premium is attached to the BriskRead account used at checkout and includes ad-free use, unlimited document length, and in-page speed reading in the Chrome extension.</li>
            <li>You must sign into that account to restore Premium on another browser or device.</li>
            <li>Account credentials are personal. Do not share, resell, or publish access to your account.</li>
            <li>If you clear browser storage, sign in again to restore account-linked access.</li>
            <li>Lifetime upgrades come with a 30-day money-back guarantee. Email billing support within 30 days of purchase for a full refund, no reason required.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>4. Limitations of Liability</h2>
          <p>
            In no event shall BriskRead or its developers be liable for any damages (including, without limitation, damages for loss of data or profit, or business interruption) arising out of the use or inability to use the speed-reading tools, even if we have been notified of the possibility of such damage.
          </p>

          <h2>5. Contact Information</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href="mailto:support@briskread.com">support@briskread.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .max-w-xl {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .content-card {
    padding: 2.5rem;
    border-radius: 1rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .content h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .content p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .content ul {
    margin-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
</style>
